window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-987f9369ea8fdebf"]={"key":"ny_b1-987f9369ea8fdebf","group":"ny_b1","uid":"987f9369ea8fdebf","rank":21,"title":"tidewater accessible inspection training geometry 01","occupation":"non_retail_sales_supervisors","archetype":"artifact_spec","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Cato Nwabueze, the first-line supervisor responsible for inspection training at Tidewater Works, and Pembroke Networks has asked for this cycle’s instructor guide and competency workbook by 4:00 p.m. on Friday for contract review. Tidewater Works supplies safety equipment under a Pembroke Networks state-agency contract, and the contract reviewer, Perpetua Lindholm, will reject the package if it does not follow the agency’s fixed accessible-document format. Last cycle’s approved package is attached as `agency_specimen.pdf`; use that file as the only source for the required wording, sequence, heading hierarchy, figure treatment, competency labels, table structure, and pagination. The specimen is the agency’s model, not background reading, so preserve its visible structure and the relationships between the guide and the matrix rather than redesigning it for convenience. Produce an instructor guide for this year’s inspection-training session and a competency matrix that an instructor can use during delivery and a reviewer can audit afterward. The guide must be a practical, reusable document rather than a narrative report: it should retain the specimen’s instructional flow, accessible heading levels, numbered figures, prompts, and competency content, while making clear where an instructor or assessor writes information and where the document reports a calculated result. The workbook must mirror the guide’s competency table cell for cell for every shared competency identifier, title, evidence description, and scoring or status field; neither file may silently add, omit, rename, or reorder a scored competency. The matrix is intended to be completed during a live inspection-training session, sometimes while the assessor is standing beside a trainee and sometimes after the session during review, so entry areas need to be obvious, writable, and distinguishable from cells that calculate or summarize information. Keep the instrument blank for use: do not insert sample trainee names, invented scores, demonstration answers, fictional dates, or completed example rows. Labels, instructions, fixed competency text, formulas, and the controls needed to use the blank instrument are not examples and should remain present. Use the specimen’s own vocabulary for statuses, fields, headings, figures, and competency identifiers; do not invent local codes or substitute synonyms. If the specimen leaves a value dependent on other entries, preserve that dependency in the workbook instead of asking the assessor to type the same result a second time. I need a defensible edition, so where the specimen permits either a compact interpretation of an instruction or a more explicit one, choose one consistently and make the choice apparent in the guide without changing the specimen’s required structure. Prioritize accessibility and auditability over decorative styling: headings must remain navigable, tables must be readable when printed, and the guide must paginate like the approved model. The package will be printed and also circulated electronically, while the workbook will be edited and printed for filing, so check both the on-screen structure and the print behavior before delivery. Write `tidewater_instructor_guide.docx` and `tidewater_competency_matrix.xlsx` into the top level of the working directory the solver starts in, using exactly those filenames. Do not include a cover letter, extra worksheets, a separate answer key, a logo, or any third file; the two named files are the complete submission.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/agency_specimen.pdf` — Approved last-cycle specimen showing the required accessible instructor-guide structure, heading hierarchy, figure numbering, pagination, and the competency matrix that the new guide and workbook must reproduce.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `tidewater_instructor_guide.docx` — Blank, accessible instructor guide for the current inspection-training cycle, structurally matching the supplied agency specimen. (Use the supplied specimen as the controlling source for wording, order, heading levels, figures, table content, and pagination.; Keep trainee-result and assessment-entry areas blank; do not add sample answers or completed examples.; Retain the specimen's competency table cell for cell and keep shared content synchronized with the workbook.; Make user-entry areas distinguishable from computed or fixed-content areas.; Deliver exactly at the top level of the starting working directory.)\n- `tidewater_competency_matrix.xlsx` — Blank competency matrix workbook for live assessment and later audit, mirroring the guide's competency table. (Use the specimen's competency identifiers, labels, order, and shared table fields exactly.; Leave all assessor-entered and trainee-result cells empty at delivery.; Use formulas for values derived from other workbook entries; do not ask users to retype computed summaries.; Preserve the specimen's status vocabulary through usable validation controls where applicable.; Configure the workbook for the specimen's required print area and pagination.; Deliver exactly at the top level of the starting working directory.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/agency_specimen.pdf","bytes":30067,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/b116c13f48766b64936d0da7b572ca9506ce7052ed82c1ca177910aef840eb50.pdf","sha256":"b116c13f48766b64936d0da7b572ca9506ce7052ed82c1ca177910aef840eb50","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"TIDEWATER WORKS | INSPECTION TRAINING                                                       Agency specimen TW-IT-042\n\n\n\n\nTidewater Works Inspection Training Instructor Guide\nPurpose and Use\nUse this guide to deliver the inspection-training session and to document an auditable competency decision. Keep\nfixed competency wording unchanged. Enter trainee, assessor, and review information only in the designated fields of\nthe competency matrix.\n\nInspection Training Overview\nThe session follows a repeatable sequence: prepare the inspection area, observe the demonstration, capture\nobjective evidence, compare evidence with the criteria, and record a result for each competency.\nBefore the Demonstration\nConfirm the equipment identity and inspection materials. Explain that evidence must be specific enough for another\nreviewer to understand what was observed. Review the four result statuses before work begins.\nDuring the Demonstration\nObserve without coaching the demonstrated step unless an immediate safety concern requires intervention. Capture\nthe condition, location, and supporting evidence. Use the same competency order in the matrix as in this guide.\n\n\n\n\nTW-IT-042                                                                                                  Page 1 of 5\n\fTIDEWATER WORKS | INSPECTION TRAINING                                                          Agency specimen TW-IT-042\n\n\n\n\nDuring delivery, the instructor keeps the observation record factual and concise. The assessor may pause the activity\nfor a safety control, then resumes the same evidence sequence.\n\n\n\n\nFigure 1: Inspection evidence flow\n\nEvidence is useful when it is observable, tied to the inspection focus, and recorded at the time of the demonstration.\nAvoid inferring competence from a general impression.\nAfter the demonstration, review each row in order. A result describes the observed performance at the time of\nassessment; it does not replace the evidence note or the follow-up record.\n\n\n\n\nTW-IT-042                                                                                                     Page 2 of 5\n\fTIDEWATER WORKS | INSPECTION TRAINING                                                         Agency specimen TW-IT-042\n\n\n\n\nEvidence and Competency Review\nRecording an Assessment\nEnter the trainee name, assessor name, and assessment date before recording results. Select one of the matrix\nstatuses: Not started, In progress, Competent, or Needs retraining. Leave a result blank until the related evidence has\nbeen reviewed.\nDuring review, the assessor enters reviewer initials and review date. The assessor also assigns the follow-up owner\nand due date when a row is not Competent. The completion rate, outstanding competencies, and overall readiness\nfields are calculated by the workbook and must not be typed.\n\n\n\n\nFigure 2: Competency decision path\n\nUse the same status vocabulary in any spoken debrief and in the matrix. If evidence is incomplete, keep the result at\nNot started or In progress until the assessor can support a decision.\n\n\n\n\nTW-IT-042                                                                                                    Page 3 of 5\n\fTIDEWATER WORKS | INSPECTION TRAINING                                                                                                         Agency specimen TW-IT-042\n\n\n\n\nEscalation and Follow-up\nWhen a defect or performance gap requires action, record the condition and assign the follow-up owner during\nreview. Set a due date that can be audited. Items marked Needs retraining remain outstanding until a later\nassessment records Competent.\nCompetency Matrix\nCompetency ID       Inspection focus                   Evidence expected                   Result      Reviewer initials   Review date   Follow-up owner   Follow-up due\n\n\n\n IT-01          Verify equipment identity and Matches\n                                              service label\n                                                       work order; label is legible and current\n\n\n IT-02          Check housing, seams, and fasteners\n                                           No cracks, loose stitching, or missing hardware\n\n\n IT-03          Inspect straps, webbing, and Webbing\n                                             adjustment\n                                                     is points\n                                                        intact; adjustments move and lock\n\n\n IT-04          Examine connectors, hooks, and\n                                           Connectors\n                                               latches close fully and show no deformation\n\n\n IT-05          Assess protective surfaces and\n                                             Surface\n                                               coatings\n                                                     is clean, continuous, and free of contamination\n\n\n IT-06          Confirm markings, warnings, and\n                                            Required\n                                                traceability\n                                                     markings are present and traceable\n\n\n IT-07          Perform functional movementMoving\n                                           check parts operate through the specified range\n\n\n IT-08          Identify defects requiring quarantine\n                                              Defects are described and item is isolated when needed\n\n\n IT-09          Record inspection evidence clearly\n                                            Notes identify condition, location, and supporting evidence\n\n\n IT-10          Communicate disposition andDisposition\n                                            escalation is stated and escalation path is followed\n\n\n\nEntry cells are shaded for assessor use; fixed competency text is retained for audit. The workbook mirrors this table cell for cell.\n\n\n\n\nTW-IT-042                                                                                                                                                       Page 4 of 5\n\f   TIDEWATER WORKS | INSPECTION TRAINING                                                                                                                                 Agency specimen TW-IT-042\n\n\n\n\nCompetency Matrix\nCompetency ID        Inspection focus                         Evidence expected                          Result   Reviewer initials   Review date   Follow-up owner   Follow-up due\n\n\n\nIT-01           Verify equipment identity and service\n                                               Matcheslabel\n                                                         work order; label is legible and current\n\n\nIT-02           Check housing, seams, and fasteners\n                                             No cracks, loose stitching, or missing hardware\n\n\nIT-03           Inspect straps, webbing, and adjustment\n                                               Webbing is\n                                                        points\n                                                          intact; adjustments move and lock\n\n\nIT-04           Examine connectors, hooks, and\n                                             Connectors\n                                               latches close fully and show no deformation\n\n\nIT-05           Assess protective surfaces and Surface\n                                               coatingsis clean, continuous, and free of contamination\n\n\nIT-06           Confirm markings, warnings, and\n                                              Required\n                                                traceability\n                                                       markings are present and traceable\n\n\nIT-07           Perform functional movement check\n                                             Moving parts operate through the specified range\n\n\nIT-08           Identify defects requiring quarantine\n                                                Defects are described and item is isolated when needed\n\n\nIT-09           Record inspection evidence clearly\n                                              Notes identify condition, location, and supporting evidence\n\n\nIT-10           Communicate disposition and escalation\n                                             Disposition is stated and escalation path is followed\n\n\n\n\n   TW-IT-042                                                                                                                                                                            Page 5 of 5\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/tidewater_competency_matrix.xlsx","bytes":8268,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/430322a8cd4787a59bd8f9b7e5501e682e10f0c76c125272517ee1575e8f5ade.xlsx","sha256":"430322a8cd4787a59bd8f9b7e5501e682e10f0c76c125272517ee1575e8f5ade","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Competency Matrix","row_count":17,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Tidewater Works Inspection Training - Competency Matrix"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Trainee name","","Assessor name","","Assessment date",""]},{"r":"4","cells":["Reviewer initials","","Review date","","Follow-up owner","","Follow-up due",""]},{"r":"6","cells":["Completion rate","=COUNTIF(D11:D20,\"Competent\")/10  [缓存: 缺失]","","Calculated fields - do not type"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Outstanding competencies","=10-COUNTIF(D11:D20,\"Competent\")  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Overall readiness","=IF(COUNTIF(D11:D20,\"Competent\")=10,\"Ready\",\"Not ready\")  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"10","cells":["Competency ID","Inspection focus","Evidence expected","Result","Reviewer initials","Review date","Follow-up owner","Follow-up due"]},{"r":"11","cells":["IT-01","Verify equipment identity and service label","Matches work order; label is legible and current","","","","",""]},{"r":"12","cells":["IT-02","Check housing, seams, and fasteners","No cracks, loose stitching, or missing hardware","","","","",""]},{"r":"13","cells":["IT-03","Inspect straps, webbing, and adjustment points","Webbing is intact; adjustments move and lock","","","","",""]},{"r":"14","cells":["IT-04","Examine connectors, hooks, and latches","Connectors close fully and show no deformation","","","","",""]},{"r":"15","cells":["IT-05","Assess protective surfaces and coatings","Surface is clean, continuous, and free of contamination","","","","",""]},{"r":"16","cells":["IT-06","Confirm markings, warnings, and traceability","Required markings are present and traceable","","","","",""]},{"r":"17","cells":["IT-07","Perform functional movement check","Moving parts operate through the specified range","","","","",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["IT-08","Identify defects requiring quarantine","Defects are described and item is isolated when needed","","","","",""]},{"r":"19","cells":["IT-09","Record inspection evidence clearly","Notes identify condition, location, and supporting evidence","","","","",""]},{"r":"20","cells":["IT-10","Communicate disposition and escalation","Disposition is stated and escalation path is followed","","","","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Instructions","row_count":6,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Instructions"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Use the Competency Matrix during the live inspection-training session and subsequent review."]},{"r":"5","cells":["Entry fields","Fixed labels and shaded cells identify where the assessor enters names, dates, statuses, initials, owners, and due dates. Leave entry cells blank until the assessment occurs."]},{"r":"8","cells":["Result statuses","Select exactly one status for each competency: Not started, In progress, Competent, or Needs retraining."]},{"r":"11","cells":["Computed summaries","Completion rate counts Competent results out of ten rows. Outstanding competencies counts every blank or non-Competent result. Overall readiness reports Ready only when all ten results are Competent; otherwise it reports Not ready. Do not type in these fields."]},{"r":"15","cells":["Follow-up","During review, the assessor assigns the follow-up owner and due date for any row that is not Competent."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/tidewater_instructor_guide.docx","bytes":56003,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/40cc633c4d2ac909e576f45ae8684ac0f6db3c89dea197ab9345593eb0f8f660.docx","sha256":"40cc633c4d2ac909e576f45ae8684ac0f6db3c89dea197ab9345593eb0f8f660","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Tidewater Works Inspection Training Instructor Guide\nPurpose and Use\nUse this guide to deliver the inspection-training session and to document an auditable competency decision. Keep fixed competency wording unchanged. Enter trainee, assessor, and review information only in the designated fields of the competency matrix.\nInspection Training Overview\nThe session follows a repeatable sequence: prepare the inspection area, observe the demonstration, capture objective evidence, compare evidence with the criteria, and record a result for each competency.\nBefore the Demonstration\nConfirm the equipment identity and inspection materials. Explain that evidence must be specific enough for another reviewer to understand what was observed. Review the four result statuses before work begins.\nDuring the Demonstration\nObserve without coaching the demonstrated step unless an immediate safety concern requires intervention. Capture the condition, location, and supporting evidence. Use the same competency order in the matrix as in this guide.\n\n\nDuring delivery, the instructor keeps the observation record factual and concise. The assessor may pause the activity for a safety control, then resumes the same evidence sequence.\n\nFigure 1: Inspection evidence flow\nEvidence is useful when it is observable, tied to the inspection focus, and recorded at the time of the demonstration. Avoid inferring competence from a general impression.\nAfter the demonstration, review each row in order. A result describes the observed performance at the time of assessment; it does not replace the evidence note or the follow-up record.\n\n\nEvidence and Competency Review\nRecording an Assessment\nEnter the trainee name, assessor name, and assessment date before recording results. Select one of the matrix statuses: Not started, In progress, Competent, or Needs retraining. Leave a result blank until the related evidence has been reviewed.\nDuring review, the assessor enters reviewer initials and review date. The assessor also assigns the follow-up owner and due date when a row is not Competent. The completion rate, outstanding competencies, and overall readiness fields are calculated by the workbook and must not be typed.\n\nFigure 2: Competency decision path\nUse the same status vocabulary in any spoken debrief and in the matrix. If evidence is incomplete, keep the result at Not started or In progress until the assessor can support a decision.\n\n\nEscalation and Follow-up\nWhen a defect or performance gap requires action, record the condition and assign the follow-up owner during review. Set a due date that can be audited. Items marked Needs retraining remain outstanding until a later assessment records Competent.\nCompetency Matrix\nCompetency ID\nInspection focus\nEvidence expected\nResult\nReviewer initials\nReview date\nFollow-up owner\nFollow-up due\nIT-01\nVerify equipment identity and service label\nMatches work order; label is legible and current\n\n\n\n\n\nIT-02\nCheck housing, seams, and fasteners\nNo cracks, loose stitching, or missing hardware\n\n\n\n\n\nIT-03\nInspect straps, webbing, and adjustment points\nWebbing is intact; adjustments move and lock\n\n\n\n\n\nIT-04\nExamine connectors, hooks, and latches\nConnectors close fully and show no deformation\n\n\n\n\n\nIT-05\nAssess protective surfaces and coatings\nSurface is clean, continuous, and free of contamination\n\n\n\n\n\nIT-06\nConfirm markings, warnings, and traceability\nRequired markings are present and traceable\n\n\n\n\n\nIT-07\nPerform functional movement check\nMoving parts operate through the specified range\n\n\n\n\n\nIT-08\nIdentify defects requiring quarantine\nDefects are described and item is isolated when needed\n\n\n\n\n\nIT-09\nRecord inspection evidence clearly\nNotes identify condition, location, and supporting evidence\n\n\n\n\n\nIT-10\nCommunicate disposition and escalation\nDisposition is stated and escalation path is followed\n\n\n\n\n\nEntry cells are shaded for assessor use; fixed competency text is retained for audit. The workbook mirrors this table cell for cell.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":2,"embedded_images":["assets/9ee14c9e7866bb3c4a8e97900a93d3a22c40446e31e09fd6e35f00406378dfa6.png","assets/d44e87d5264cf38c7509840969869c85e3e9085cdf4238080bcd48ae43d5c84d.png"]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"r01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The instructor guide is a DOCX and contains the required title and all specimen-defined instructional sections.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Document XML and rendered guide","grader_hint":"Extract paragraph text and compare required titles and section wording with agency_specimen.pdf."},{"rubric_item_id":"r02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The instructor guide renders to exactly 4 Letter portrait pages.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX PDF","grader_hint":"Render offline and inspect page size, orientation, and page count with pypdf."},{"rubric_item_id":"r03","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Guide page margins match the specimen within ±0.05 inch on each side.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX section properties","grader_hint":"Read section margin properties and compare with the supplied specimen."},{"rubric_item_id":"r04","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The guide uses the specimen's heading levels for every required heading.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX paragraph styles","grader_hint":"Inspect paragraph styles or outline levels; do not rely only on visual bolding."},{"rubric_item_id":"r05","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The guide contains Figure 1 and Figure 2 with the specimen's exact captions and numbering.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX captions and rendered pages","grader_hint":"Extract captions and verify numbering and caption text against the PDF."},{"rubric_item_id":"r06","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Figure 1 and Figure 2 appear on the same specimen-designated pages and do not move across page boundaries.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered guide PDF","grader_hint":"Map figure captions to rendered page numbers and compare with the specimen."},{"rubric_item_id":"r07","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The guide has a navigable heading outline containing the specimen's required hierarchy.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX styles and outline levels","grader_hint":"Confirm Heading 1 and Heading 2 levels are structurally assigned and ordered."},{"rubric_item_id":"r08","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The guide contains the complete eight-column competency table with the specimen's headers in order.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX table XML","grader_hint":"Inspect the table grid and first-row text, not only the rendered appearance."},{"rubric_item_id":"r09","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The guide competency table contains exactly 10 competency rows and 8 columns.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX table geometry","grader_hint":"Count table rows and columns from the DOCX XML."},{"rubric_item_id":"r10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every guide competency row has the same ID, fixed wording, and order as the supplied specimen.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Guide table versus source PDF","grader_hint":"Extract all ten rows and compare normalized cell text row by row."},{"rubric_item_id":"r11","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The guide distinguishes fixed instructional content from assessor-entry areas using the specimen's intended labels and affordances.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered guide and document structure","grader_hint":"Check that entry cells are visibly identifiable and fixed competency text is not presented as an editable result."},{"rubric_item_id":"r12","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The guide states the chosen follow-up ownership interpretation consistently with the supplied matrix fields.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Guide recording instruction","grader_hint":"Find an explicit instruction assigning follow-up ownership during review; accept equivalent professional wording."},{"rubric_item_id":"r13","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook opens successfully and contains sheets named Competency Matrix and Instructions in that order.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"XLSX workbook metadata","grader_hint":"Open with openpyxl and inspect sheetnames."},{"rubric_item_id":"r14","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook matrix is exactly 8 columns by 10 competency rows beneath its header.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worksheet dimensions","grader_hint":"Identify the matrix header and count its data rows and columns."},{"rubric_item_id":"r15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Workbook competency IDs, fixed wording, headers, and row order match the guide cell for cell.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Both submitted files","grader_hint":"Normalize and compare all 80 shared table cells; allow only formatting differences."},{"rubric_item_id":"r16","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains the specimen's eight matrix headers in the specified order.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worksheet header row","grader_hint":"Read header cells from the matrix sheet."},{"rubric_item_id":"r17","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook includes separate entry fields for trainee name, assessor name, and assessment date.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worksheet labels and cells","grader_hint":"Locate labeled fields and verify they are distinct from computed summary fields."},{"rubric_item_id":"r18","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook includes separate entry fields for reviewer initials, review date, follow-up owner, and follow-up due.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Matrix columns and worksheet labels","grader_hint":"Verify each required field is present and has an associated blank input cell."},{"rubric_item_id":"r19","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every Result cell has a data-validation dropdown whose candidates are exactly Not started, In progress, Competent, and Needs retraining.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"XLSX dataValidation XML","grader_hint":"Inspect validation ranges and formulas; accept blank as an allowed initial state."},{"rubric_item_id":"r20","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Date entry cells use date validation that permits blank cells and rejects non-date values.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"XLSX dataValidation XML","grader_hint":"Inspect validation type, allow_blank, and target ranges."},{"rubric_item_id":"r21","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains a Completion rate summary field with a formula rather than a constant.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook formula cells","grader_hint":"Load with data_only=False and verify a formula references all ten Result cells."},{"rubric_item_id":"r22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Completion rate is calculated as the count of Competent results divided by the ten competency rows, with blanks not counted as competent.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Formula expression","grader_hint":"Evaluate or inspect the formula logic; accept equivalent formulas covering all ten rows."},{"rubric_item_id":"r23","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Completion rate cell uses a percentage number format.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cell number_format","grader_hint":"Inspect the summary cell format."},{"rubric_item_id":"r24","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains an Outstanding competencies summary field with a formula.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook formula cells","grader_hint":"Verify the cell is formula-backed and references the Result range."},{"rubric_item_id":"r25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Outstanding competencies counts every blank or non-Competent Result and does not count a Competent result.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Formula expression","grader_hint":"Test formula logic against blank, each listed status, and Competent."},{"rubric_item_id":"r26","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains an Overall readiness summary field with a formula and no independent input control.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook XML and validation ranges","grader_hint":"Confirm formula presence and that the cell is not part of user-entry validation."},{"rubric_item_id":"r27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Overall readiness reports Ready only when all ten Result cells equal Competent and otherwise reports Not ready.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Formula expression","grader_hint":"Test all-Competent, partially completed, blank, and Needs retraining cases."},{"rubric_item_id":"r28","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook visibly separates user-entry cells from fixed labels and computed summary cells.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered workbook and cell styles","grader_hint":"Inspect fills, borders, protection, or legend cues and verify the distinction is consistent."},{"rubric_item_id":"r29","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook includes an Instructions sheet explaining how to enter results and interpret computed summaries.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Instructions sheet text","grader_hint":"Check for concise operational instructions covering entry versus computed fields."},{"rubric_item_id":"r30","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The matrix header row is frozen for navigation during assessment.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worksheet freeze_panes","grader_hint":"Inspect freeze_panes and verify it freezes the matrix header."},{"rubric_item_id":"r31","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook print paper is Letter and orientation is landscape.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worksheet page setup","grader_hint":"Inspect paperSize and orientation."},{"rubric_item_id":"r32","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook is configured to fit the complete matrix and summary block to one page wide and one page tall.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worksheet page setup and print area","grader_hint":"Inspect fitToWidth, fitToHeight, fitToPage, and print_area."},{"rubric_item_id":"r33","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook print area contains the complete matrix and summary block and no unrelated blank region.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worksheet print_area","grader_hint":"Compare the defined print range with used cells and required summary boundaries."},{"rubric_item_id":"r34","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook uses the specimen-consistent date format for all date fields.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cell number formats","grader_hint":"Compare date number formats with the specimen's displayed convention."},{"rubric_item_id":"r35","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All ten Result cells are empty at delivery while retaining their validation controls.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cell values and validation XML","grader_hint":"Check values with data_only=False and validation coverage."},{"rubric_item_id":"r36","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All identity, date, initials, owner, and due-date entry cells are empty at delivery.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook cell values","grader_hint":"Inspect every designated entry cell for absence of text, numbers, and formulas."},{"rubric_item_id":"r37","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The guide contains no invented completed assessment values or sample trainee information.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered guide and document text","grader_hint":"Check entry cells and instructional examples; fixed labels and formulas are acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"r38","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The guide's matrix and workbook use the same four status terms without synonym drift.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Both files and workbook validation","grader_hint":"Compare status vocabulary in guide instructions, matrix, and validation list."},{"rubric_item_id":"r39","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The guide's competency table appears on the same designated page and occupies the same structural position relative to surrounding content as the specimen.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered guide versus source PDF","grader_hint":"Compare page number and neighboring headings/table boundaries."},{"rubric_item_id":"r40","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The guide and workbook preserve all ten competency identifiers exactly, with no duplicates or omissions.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Both files","grader_hint":"Extract identifier sets and compare to the source and each other."},{"rubric_item_id":"r41","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The guide has accessible document properties and semantic table header information sufficient for navigation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX XML","grader_hint":"Inspect heading styles, table header row marking, and document core properties."},{"rubric_item_id":"r42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"An instructor can identify what to fill in, what the statuses mean, and which summary values should not be typed without asking for help.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered guide and workbook used as a blank instrument","grader_hint":"Have a reviewer unfamiliar with the construction attempt a blank assessment using only the two files; award when the distinction and instructions are immediately clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"r43","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The two files look and read like one agency-issued package rather than two independently designed artifacts.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX and XLSX","grader_hint":"Judge consistency of terminology, hierarchy, table labels, spacing, and print usability against the supplied specimen."},{"rubric_item_id":"r44","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Both deliverables open without repair prompts and the workbook formulas, validation lists, and print settings remain present after save and reopen.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Offline open/reopen test","grader_hint":"Open with standard office libraries and, where available, a headless office renderer; inspect XML after reopening."},{"rubric_item_id":"r45","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submission contains exactly the two required files at the top level and no extra deliverable files.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Working-directory file listing","grader_hint":"Check exact filenames and extensions; ignore temporary process files outside the submitted package."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Enterprise safety-equipment training is being packaged for a state-agency contract review. The files must be usable by instructors during assessment and credible to an external compliance reviewer who compares them with the approved specimen.","difficulty_sources":["Reconstructing a fixed accessible document structure from one supplied specimen without drifting in heading hierarchy, figure numbering, pagination, or table content.","Choosing and documenting a consistent interpretation where the specimen permits two defensible readings while preserving the agency's required structure.","Keeping a blank instructor instrument distinct from computed workbook fields and maintaining cell-for-cell agreement across two file formats.","Making the guide and workbook practical for live assessment and later external review rather than merely visually similar."],"authoring_plan":{"source_construction":{"filename":"agency_specimen.pdf","type":"single supplied reference","purpose":"Create one five-page approved specimen PDF containing the complete instructor guide on pages 1-4 and the competency matrix specimen on page 5. Use stable synthetic content about safety-equipment inspection training. The PDF must be visually clear and extractable offline.","guide_geometry":{"page_size":"Letter","orientation":"portrait","page_count":4,"margins":"0.65 inch left and right, 0.7 inch top and bottom","header_footer":"header on every page; footer with specimen page number and fixed agency document identifier","heading_sequence":["Title","Heading 1: Purpose and Use","Heading 1: Inspection Training Overview","Heading 2: Before the Demonstration","Heading 2: During the Demonstration","Heading 1: Evidence and Competency Review","Heading 2: Recording an Assessment","Heading 1: Escalation and Follow-up"],"figures":["Figure 1: Inspection evidence flow","Figure 2: Competency decision path"],"table":{"name":"Competency Matrix","rows":10,"columns":8,"columns_in_order":["Competency ID","Inspection focus","Evidence expected","Result","Reviewer initials","Review date","Follow-up owner","Follow-up due"],"shared_rows":"Ten synthetic competency rows with unique identifiers and fixed wording. All eight columns appear in the guide table and must be reproduced in the workbook."}},"workbook_specimen":{"sheet_names_in_order":["Competency Matrix","Instructions"],"matrix_geometry":"The competency table is exactly 8 columns by 10 competency rows beneath its header, with the same ten rows and eight field labels as the guide.","summary_area":"A summary block contains three computed fields: Completion rate, Outstanding competencies, and Overall readiness. It is visibly separate from assessor-entry cells.","entry_fields":["Trainee name","Assessor name","Assessment date","Result cells for the ten competency rows","Reviewer initials","Review date","Follow-up owner","Follow-up due"],"computed_fields":["Completion rate derived from the ten Result cells","Outstanding competencies derived from the ten Result cells","Overall readiness derived from the Result cells and the specimen's status vocabulary"],"validation":{"result_column":["Not started","In progress","Competent","Needs retraining"],"date_fields":"Date validation allowing blank cells and valid dates only"},"print":{"paper":"Letter","orientation":"landscape","fit_to_width":1,"fit_to_height":1,"print_area":"The complete matrix and summary block only","repeat_rows":"The matrix header row repeats if a renderer expands the print area"},"freeze_panes":"Freeze the competency header row and the identifying columns needed to follow a row during entry.","number_formats":{"completion_rate":"percentage","dates":"date format consistent with the specimen"}},"blank_policy":"All user-entry cells, including trainee and assessor identity, dates, result selections, initials, owners, and due dates, must contain no text, number, or formula in the reference gold. Fixed labels and formulas in computed cells are allowed. No example values are to be placed in either deliverable.","derived_logic":{"completion_rate":"Count competency Result cells equal to the specimen's Competent status divided by the number of competency rows; blank results are not counted as competent.","outstanding_competencies":"Count competency Result cells that are blank, Not started, In progress, or Needs retraining.","overall_readiness":"Report Ready only when every competency Result is Competent; otherwise report Not ready. The readiness field must be formula-driven and must not be independently editable."},"cross_file_truth":"The ten competency IDs, the eight table headers, row order, fixed competency wording, and status vocabulary are identical between the guide and workbook. The guide is the rendered instructional presentation; the workbook is the operational matrix. Any shared table cell disagreement fails its corresponding cross-deliverable checks.","judgment_choice":"The specimen intentionally permits either of two defensible treatments of follow-up ownership: leaving ownership entirely for the assessor or allowing the instructor to assign it during review. The gold chooses assessor entry during review and states that choice once in the guide's recording instruction, without changing the table structure.","gold_generation":"Build the specimen PDF, then create a reference DOCX and XLSX from the same canonical competency data. Render the DOCX to PDF offline if available and inspect page count and page boundaries with pypdf. Inspect the XLSX with openpyxl for formulas, validation, print settings, dimensions, blank input cells, and sheet order. Confirm the reference solution satisfies every rubric item before setting reference_solution_passed_rubric to true."}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"required_sections"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"agency_specimen","filename":"agency_specimen.pdf","purpose":"Approved last-cycle specimen showing the required accessible instructor-guide structure, heading hierarchy, figure numbering, pagination, and the competency matrix that the new guide and workbook must reproduce.","required":true,"discovery":"Open the supplied PDF and inspect all pages, headings, figures, table cells, labels, and page boundaries before constructing either deliverable."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"instructor_guide","filename":"tidewater_instructor_guide.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"Blank, accessible instructor guide for the current inspection-training cycle, structurally matching the supplied agency specimen.","required":true,"constraints":["Use the supplied specimen as the controlling source for wording, order, heading levels, figures, table content, and pagination.","Keep trainee-result and assessment-entry areas blank; do not add sample answers or completed examples.","Retain the specimen's competency table cell for cell and keep shared content synchronized with the workbook.","Make user-entry areas distinguishable from computed or fixed-content areas.","Deliver exactly at the top level of the starting working directory."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"competency_matrix","filename":"tidewater_competency_matrix.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"Blank competency matrix workbook for live assessment and later audit, mirroring the guide's competency table.","required":true,"constraints":["Use the specimen's competency identifiers, labels, order, and shared table fields exactly.","Leave all assessor-entered and trainee-result cells empty at delivery.","Use formulas for values derived from other workbook entries; do not ask users to retype computed summaries.","Preserve the specimen's status vocabulary through usable validation controls where applicable.","Configure the workbook for the specimen's required print area and pagination.","Deliver exactly at the top level of the starting working directory."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"inspect_quality","work_product":"training_material","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"artifact_spec@v4","occupation":"non_retail_sales_supervisors","sector":"wholesale_trade","task_archetype":"artifact_spec","estimated_professional_hours":6.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"A reference script checks DOCX/XLSX structure, formulas, validations, dimensions, blankness, cross-file cell equality, and print properties; an independent document reviewer checks rendered pagination, accessibility, and practical usability.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["DOCX pagination can vary slightly across office renderers, so geometry checks should use the nominated offline renderer and the stated tolerance for margins.","Formula results may not be recalculated by openpyxl alone; formula presence and an offline spreadsheet-renderer test are both used."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:39:18+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:39:18+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:39:18+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:39:18+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:39:18+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/987f9369ea8fdebf","declared_deliverables":["tidewater_instructor_guide.docx","tidewater_competency_matrix.xlsx"]};
